{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"file-manager","displayName":"File Manager","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/russellfei/skills/file-manager","publisherHandle":"russellfei","publisherDisplayName":"russellfei","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/russellfei","version":"1.2.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1774418743565,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/file-manager/card?ownerHandle=russellfei&version=1.2.0","sha256":"39a07dddbad2534b1cbca48ed17b50e92064a74407d88920aabdd1e6417079c0","size":2460,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"11828604fe701ebf9a2dcfccb019dcd3526e8e95f1f2f5186f0e8ffae23fd7d8","bundleFingerprints":["1a5250c5ae44668dd76a73f18be7e2caf4c7da0ddc62b24930ffad4342fb4f97","387f0871a72dd09d737ef65b114ea13bf1a97c1d149c79dc6c0216561d20e511"],"files":[{"path":"references/best_practices.md","size":1921,"sha256":"32e6276249a3932e2ff02274be41f76ef3c88e68ea71fb2e13d9330eb09aea8e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":106,"sha256":"e3e23d07de4f7a1793b5152d7d8ae691460418f3ea7815df68cd458115ae9d61","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/batch_rename.py","size":7412,"sha256":"b38010f07266f9bdad52f326ae09f553d1ca5c4f2863b2e58db5375e85e2c235","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/deduplicate.py","size":7207,"sha256":"73744f2f5ace3b7af1f95870e318e6cbfd5a12814f42f82f1994cfbe51e55a2c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/organize.py","size":8004,"sha256":"260efff4203e01a906b25fd81c7cd36c67194b1b74ca50ca242d47766b241684","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/sync.py","size":6671,"sha256":"ee2d78796f063138d33bfb27b222b78ceb66d2b08f1cc7e51c3aa68010440b0b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/utils.py","size":652,"sha256":"27bbddf2198f0450675697e83ef0b42c9f1fa90bf526296ec60579c506e68cd7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3690,"sha256":"f99bca566fe4df715309b87ed7ec36dd69a6706ca7c3f6d1b8ae6c8123366676","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent file manager, but it needs Review because its bulk rename and sync commands can unexpectedly move or delete user files outside the intended scope.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789099672801,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Path Traversal in Batch Rename Destination"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/batch_rename.py"},"region":{"startLine":49,"endLine":212}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"43f36d66576b7eef"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/batch_rename.py`, lines 49-91 and 184-212  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Unrestricted destination path construction  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\nfor i, file_path in enumerate(files, 1):\n    old_name = file_path.name\n    new_name = old_name\n\n    # Add prefix\n    if kwargs.get('prefix'):\n        new_name = kwargs['prefix'] + new_name\n\n    # Add suffix\n    if kwargs.get('suffix'):\n        stem = Path(new_name).stem\n        suffix = kwargs['suffix']\n        ext = Path(new_name).suffix\n        new_name = f\"{stem}{suffix}{ext}\"\n\n    # Regex replacement\n    if kwargs.get('replace_pattern') and kwargs.get('replace_with') is not None:\n        try:\n            regex = re.compile(kwargs['replace_pattern'])\n            new_name = regex.sub(kwargs['replace_with'], new_name)\n        except re.error as e:\n            print(f\"Regular expression error: {e}\")\n            return []\n\n    # Sequence rename\n    if kwargs.get('sequence'):\n        template = kwargs.get('sequence_template', 'file_{n}')\n        padding = kwargs.get('padding', 3)\n        ext = file_path.suffix\n        new_name = generate_sequence_name(template, i, padding) + ext\n\n    if new_name != old_name:\n        operations.append((file_path, file_path.parent / new_name))\n```\n\nThe preview and execution logic are:\n\n```python\nfor old_path, new_path in operations:\n    print(f\"  {old_path.name}\")\n    print(f\"    → {new_path.name}\\n\")\n\nif not args.execute:\n    print(\"This is a preview. Use --execute to perform the actual rename.\")\n    return\n\nif not args.no_confirm:\n    confirm = input(\"\\nConfirm rename? (yes/no): \")\n    if confirm.lower() != 'yes':\n        print(\"Operation cancelled\")\n        return\n\nfor old_path, new_path in operations:\n    try:\n        if new_path.exists():\n            print(f\"Skipped {old_path.name}: destination already exists\")\n            failed += 1\n            continue\n        old_path.rename(new_path)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe prefix, regular-expression replacement, and sequence template are user-controlled and are incorporated into `new_name` without validating that the result is a single filename. Directory separators, `..` path components, and absolute paths are not rejected.\n\nThe expression:\n\n```python\nfile_path.parent / new_name\n```\n\ndoes not guarantee that the resulting path remains under `file_path.parent`. A relative value containing `../` can traverse to another directory, while an absolute `new_name` causes `pathlib` to discard the preceding parent path entirely.\n\nThe preview only displays `new_path.name`, rather than the complete destination path. Consequently, path traversal components and an unexpected destination directory may not be visible to a user reviewing the operation.\n\nThe destination must already have an existing parent directory because the rename script does not create it. Existing destination files are skipped, so this issue does not directly overwrite an existing regular file through the normal execution path.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker or unsafe automation supplies a rename option containing path components, such as a prefix, replacement, or sequence template with `../`.\n2. Matching files are selected from a directory writable by the current user.\n3. The script constructs destinations outside the selected directory.\n4. The preview displays only the destination basename, concealing the effective parent directory.\n5. The operation is invoked with `--execute`.\n6. The user approves the operation, or `--no-confirm` is supplied.\n7. `Path.rename()` moves each selected file to the out-of-scope destination.\n\nAn illustrative invocation is:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/batch_rename.py \"*.txt\" \\\n  --dir ./documents \\\n  --prefix \"../archive/\" \\\n  --execute \\\n  --no-confirm\n```\n\nIf `./archive` exists relative to the selected files, matching files can be moved outside `./documents`.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe vulnerability permits file movement outside the user-selected rename directory. Its scope is limited to locations accessible to the operating-system account running the Skill; it does not provide privilege escalation or access beyond that account's permissions.\n\nPotential consequences include:\n\n- Unexpected relocation or loss of access to selected files.\n- Modification of file layouts outside the declared working directory.\n- Placement of files into attacker-chosen writable directories.\n- Misleading preview output that prevents informed confirmation.\n- Disruption of applications that depend on the original file paths.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Require the generated value to be a filename, not a path:\n   - Reject `/` and `\\`.\n   - Reject `.` and `..`.\n   - Reject absolute paths.\n   - Reject any value for which `Path(new_name).name != new_name`.\n\n2. Resolve and validate every destination before adding it to the operation list:\n\n```python\nbase_dir = file_path.parent.resolve()\ncandidate = file_path.parent / new_name\n\nif Path(new_name).is_absolute():\n    raise ValueError(\"Absolute destination paths are not allowed\")\n\nresolved_candidate = candidate.resolve(strict=False)\nif resolved_candidate.parent != base_dir:\n    raise ValueError(\"Destination must remain in the source file's directory\")\n```\n\n3. Display the complete source and destination paths in the preview:\n\n```python\nprint(f\"{old_path.resolve()} -> {new_path.resolve(strict=False)}\")\n```\n\n4. Abort execution when destination collisions are detected instead of merely warning.\n\n5. Consider removing `--no-confirm`. If non-interactive operation is required, require an additional explicit safety option after all paths have passed containment validation.\n\n6. Revalidate containment immediately before `rename()` to reduce time-of-check/time-of-use risks caused by filesystem changes.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Overlapping Synchronization Roots Can Delete Source Files or Cause Recursive Copy Growth"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/sync.py"},"region":{"startLine":35,"endLine":142}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"d93d87fc496379c5"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/sync.py`, lines 35-142  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Missing source and target path-separation validation  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```python\ndef sync_mirror(source, target, exclude=None, dry_run=True, delete=False):\n    \"\"\"One-way mirror synchronization (source → target)\"\"\"\n    source_path = Path(source)\n    target_path = Path(target)\n    exclude = exclude or []\n\n    if not source_path.exists():\n        print(f\"Error: source directory does not exist: {source}\")\n        return\n\n    target_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    stats = {'copied': 0, 'updated': 0, 'deleted': 0, 'skipped': 0}\n\n    # Obtain source files\n    source_files = {}\n    for file_path in source_path.rglob('*'):\n        if file_path.is_symlink():\n            continue\n        if file_path.is_file() and not should_exclude(\n                file_path, exclude, base_path=source_path):\n            rel_path = file_path.relative_to(source_path)\n            source_files[rel_path] = file_path\n\n    # Obtain target files\n    target_files = {}\n    for file_path in target_path.rglob('*'):\n        if file_path.is_symlink():\n            continue\n        if file_path.is_file() and not should_exclude(\n                file_path, exclude, base_path=target_path):\n            rel_path = file_path.relative_to(target_path)\n            target_files[rel_path] = file_path\n```\n\nDeletion actions are generated and executed without first proving that the target is separate from the source:\n\n```python\nif delete:\n    for rel_path, tgt_file in target_files.items():\n        if rel_path not in source_files:\n            actions.append(('delete', None, tgt_file))\n```\n\n```python\nfor action, src, tgt in actions:\n    try:\n        tgt.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n        if action == 'copy':\n            shutil.copy2(src, tgt)\n            stats['copied'] += 1\n        elif action == 'update':\n            shutil.copy2(src, tgt)\n            stats['updated'] += 1\n        elif action == 'delete':\n            tgt.unlink()\n            stats['deleted'] += 1\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe synchronization function accepts arbitrary source and target directories but does not resolve and compare them. It therefore permits:\n\n- Source and target to be identical.\n- Source to be nested inside target.\n- Target to be nested inside source.\n- Lexically different paths that resolve to overlapping locations.\n\nWhen the source is inside the target, source files appear in the target scan under an additional path prefix. With `--delete`, those entries may not exist in `source_files` under the same relative names, causing genuine source files to be classified as target-only files and deleted.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\ntarget: /backup\nsource: /backup/work\nfile:   /backup/work/report.txt\n```\n\nThe source scan records `report.txt`, while the target scan records the same physical file as `work/report.txt`. Since `work/report.txt` is not a source-relative key, it is scheduled for deletion.\n\nWhen the target is inside the source, the source traversal includes existing target content. Files from that target subtree can then be copied into another nested target subtree. Repeated runs can produce progressively deeper directory structures and excessive storage consumption.\n\nThe dry-run default and interactive confirmation reduce accidental activation, but they do not correct the unsafe action plan. The preview also displays only the first 20 operations, so a large destructive plan may not be fully visible.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n#### Source deletion through a parent target\n\n1. Place or select the source directory inside the target directory.\n2. Run mirror synchronization with deletion and execution enabled:\n\n```bash\npython scripts/sync.py /backup/work /backup \\\n  --mirror \\\n  --delete \\\n  --execute\n```\n\n3. The source scan indexes `/backup/work/report.txt` as `report.txt`.\n4. The target scan indexes the same file as `work/report.txt`.\n5. The deletion planner treats `work/report.txt` as absent from the source map.\n6. The user confirms the synchronization operation.\n7. `tgt.unlink()` deletes `/backup/work/report.txt`, which is an actual source file.\n\n#### Recursive copy growth through a child target\n\n1. Select a target directory nested within the source.\n2. Run synchronization repeatedly.\n3. Each source scan includes files already stored below the target.\n4. Those entries are copied into deeper paths under the target.\n5. Repeated runs can increase directory depth and consume additional storage.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe operation runs with the permissions of the invoking operating-system account. It does not escalate privileges, but it can affect any readable or writable paths selected by that account.\n\nPotential consequences include:\n\n- Permanent deletion of source files when `--delete` is enabled.\n- Corruption of backup or synchronization layouts.\n- Repeated replication and uncontrolled storage consumption.\n- Overwriting of target files during update operations.\n- Loss of data availability within the full selected directory trees.\n- Increased risk when the script is scheduled unattended using the documented automation pattern.\n  ]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Resolve both roots before creating the target or scanning either directory:\n\n```python\nsource_path = Path(source).expanduser().resolve(strict=True)\ntarget_path = Path(target).expanduser().resolve(strict=False)\n```\n\n2. Reject identical and overlapping roots:\n\n```python\ndef is_relative_to(path, parent):\n    try:\n        path.relative_to(parent)\n        return True\n    except ValueError:\n        return False\n\nif source_path == target_path:\n    raise ValueError(\"Source and target must be different directories\")\n\nif is_relative_to(source_path, target_path):\n    raise ValueError(\"Source cannot be inside target\")\n\nif is_relative_to(target_path, source_path):\n    raise ValueError(\"Target cannot be inside source\")\n```\n\n3. For destructive synchronization, reject dangerous targets such as a filesystem root or user home directory unless a narrowly scoped, explicit override is supplied.\n\n4. Before every copy, update, or deletion, resolve the destination and verify that it remains below the validated target root.\n\n5. Before deletion, explicitly verify that the candidate is not within the resolved source root.\n\n6. Abort if either root changes identity during execution. Where practical, use file descriptors or platform-specific safe traversal mechanisms to reduce symlink and time-of-check/time-of-use risks.\n\n7. Show the complete action list for deletion operations, or export it to a reviewable manifest. Require a stronger confirmation that states the number and root location of files to be deleted.\n\n8. Add automated tests for:\n   - Identical source and target.\n   - Source nested inside target.\n   - Target nested inside source.\n   - Paths containing `..`.\n   - Paths resolving through symlinks.\n   - Filesystem-root targets.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":35,"primaryLanguage":"Python","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789099526.3070767,"endTime":1789099629.103106}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"file-manager","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v574h7b80j2bj0w0m83bg95mnx8e6mk6-pZQeLp/clawscan-skillspector-2785852892/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-11T04:05:25.250602+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":135,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3690,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/best_practices.md","type":"markdown","lines":77,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1921,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"requirements.txt","type":"text","lines":2,"executable":false,"size_bytes":106,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/batch_rename.py","type":"python","lines":223,"executable":true,"size_bytes":7412,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/deduplicate.py","type":"python","lines":205,"executable":true,"size_bytes":7207,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/organize.py","type":"python","lines":213,"executable":true,"size_bytes":8004,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/sync.py","type":"python","lines":190,"executable":true,"size_bytes":6671,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/utils.py","type":"python","lines":24,"executable":true,"size_bytes":652,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"TP4","finding_id":"finding-3940d0aea24242b6b86c41d7ef8ee1d5","category":"MCP Tool Poisoning","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code is clearly related to file management and does perform one subset of the declared description: intelligent file classification/organization. However, the declared purpose describes a broader automation assistant supporting batch operations, duplicate cleanup, renaming, directory sync, and automated workflows. This code chunk only implements organization by type or date, plus copy/move into category folders. It does not perform duplicate detection/removal, explicit batch renaming, directory synchronization, or broader workflow automation. Additionally, although the CLI advertises --by-size, that feature is only a placeholder ('开发中...') and not functional. Therefore the description materially overstates the implemented capabilities, creating a description-behavior mismatch.","remediation":"Update the skill description to accurately reflect all capabilities, or remove undeclared functionality from the implementation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02","AML.T0080","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"code_path":"scripts/organize.py","code_start_line":1,"code_end_line":213,"actual_behavior_summary":"A command-line script that organizes files in a source directory by file type or modification date, with preview mode, optional copy/move execution, and confirmation prompts. Size-based organization is declared in CLI options but not implemented."},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-961e353f1c08453da04e4a99f8473f6a","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/sync.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/sync.py <source> <target> --mirror","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7e930d556c462a5c018abdf485d66002b98e30e1510797dc632a76dedd575406","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":57,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-961e353f1c08453da04e4a99f8473f6a","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":60,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/sync.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/sync.py <source> <target> --mirror","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7e930d556c462a5c018abdf485d66002b98e30e1510797dc632a76dedd575406","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":60,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-961e353f1c08453da04e4a99f8473f6a","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/sync.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/sync.py <source> <target> --mirror","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7e930d556c462a5c018abdf485d66002b98e30e1510797dc632a76dedd575406","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-961e353f1c08453da04e4a99f8473f6a","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":91,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/sync.py (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"python scripts/sync.py <source> <target> --mirror","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7e930d556c462a5c018abdf485d66002b98e30e1510797dc632a76dedd575406","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":91,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-08d2af9f3aff4509b2f804ad61b79321","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"scripts/batch_rename.py","start_line":155,"end_line":null},"finding":"--no-confirm","explanation":"The tool allows destructive filesystem changes to proceed non-interactively via --execute --no-confirm, with user-controlled patterns and rename templates. In an agent skill context, this increases the risk of parameter abuse: a mistaken or malicious invocation can mass-rename files at scale without a human checkpoint, causing operational disruption or data handling errors.","remediation":"Restrict non-interactive execution in agent contexts by disallowing --no-confirm unless an explicit trusted automation mode is enabled. Add path allowlists, scope limits on the number of files affected, collision/finality checks that abort on conflicts, and require a positive acknowledgement token or policy gate before bulk renames are executed.","code_snippet":"                       help='转换为大写')\n    parser.add_argument('--execute', action='store_true',\n                       help='执行重命名 (默认仅预览)')\n    parser.add_argument('--no-confirm', action='store_true',\n                       help='跳过确认')\n    \n    args = parser.parse_args()","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d4a5ab8fab96e8499b30127e14cd8403ee849aa299b11cdf650900635b20f465","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/batch_rename.py","start_line":155,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-a2b6a0eb56cd4be7be288256ea00f906","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill advertises and instructs file-modifying operations but does not declare any explicit tool scope such as permissions or allowed-tools. That creates an authorization ambiguity where an agent may invoke file-write capabilities more broadly than intended, increasing the chance of unintended or unsafe filesystem changes.","remediation":"Add explicit permission metadata defining the minimum required tool scope, especially file read/write limitations and path boundaries. Restrict operations to approved directories, document destructive capabilities clearly, and require explicit user confirmation plus dry-run behavior for write/delete actions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-15f0bb859ac7484d8ddf3f440ffe9609","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The activation description is broad enough to trigger on many ordinary file-related requests, which can cause the skill to be selected in situations the user did not specifically intend. In a file-management context, overbroad invocation is risky because the skill includes write, move, delete, and sync workflows that could alter user data.","remediation":"Narrow the activation criteria to explicit tasks such as organizing a specified directory, deduplicating with confirmation, or syncing named paths. Add gating language that requires clear user intent for destructive or bulk file operations before the skill is invoked.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-8fc6c41a1fc44acea877ab5956941fc9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":57},"finding":null,"explanation":"The examples prominently show destructive operations such as deleting duplicate files and mirroring directories without adjacent, explicit warnings about irreversible data loss. In a filesystem-management skill, copy-pastable destructive commands materially increase the risk of accidental deletion, overwrite, or propagation of mistakes across directories.","remediation":"Add strong user-facing warnings next to delete and mirror examples, make dry-run examples the default, and require explicit backup or confirmation guidance before showing destructive commands. Prefer quarantine/move examples over delete, and document rollback or recovery steps where possible.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":45,"end_line":57}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3e7c3678af654864a5827e2cc1222f46","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"references/best_practices.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"The guidance '中文文件名（某些系统兼容性问题）' is presented as a blanket rule in a Chinese-language document, effectively imposing a language-related naming restriction. The file does not frame this as optional, context-dependent, or limited to environments with demonstrated compatibility issues.","remediation":"Revise the guidance to explain that non-ASCII filenames may cause compatibility issues in some systems, and present it as a conditional recommendation rather than a blanket prohibition; offer users a choice based on their target environment.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/best_practices.md","start_line":15,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-023cdaaafad24184af71bad9dc04fd63","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/best_practices.md","start_line":46,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document provides destructive or state-changing automation examples such as `--mirror`, `--move`, and `--execute` for backup and file organization without prominent warnings about deletion, overwrite, or unintended file movement. In a file-management skill, users are likely to copy these commands directly, so unsafe examples can cause accidental data loss even if the content is not overtly malicious.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings before every state-changing example explaining that `--mirror` may delete destination files and `--move` relocates files. Provide safer dry-run examples first, such as preview mode without `--execute`, recommend testing on sample directories, and document backup/recovery steps before running automation on real data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/best_practices.md","start_line":46,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-fd83bea128bf4e6ebcd105f824bd2650","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"scripts/batch_rename.py","start_line":3,"end_line":154},"finding":null,"explanation":"The natural-language content presented to users, including the module description, CLI help text, prompts, and status messages, is entirely in Chinese. This imposes a specific language on users without offering a language choice or documenting a justified region-specific constraint, which matches the locale-policy violation criteria.","remediation":"Add multilingual support or an explicit language-selection option for user-facing messages. If the tool is intentionally Chinese-only, document that locale constraint clearly in the skill description and justify the regional scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/batch_rename.py","start_line":3,"end_line":154}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-cfb9b01718264c1eaac3a3aabc33817a","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.65,"location":{"file":"scripts/batch_rename.py","start_line":155,"end_line":null},"finding":"--no-confirm","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"                       help='转换为大写')\n    parser.add_argument('--execute', action='store_true',\n                       help='执行重命名 (默认仅预览)')\n    parser.add_argument('--no-confirm', action='store_true',\n                       help='跳过确认')\n    \n    args = parser.parse_args()","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"9330f9b4da2a4918ec7c8cb13448914cfc40e475b60578e278be9d82eec87807","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/batch_rename.py","start_line":155,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f23ec2128f6a4183a09480201b36d32d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/deduplicate.py","start_line":3,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The module docstring and all user-facing CLI descriptions are written only in Chinese, indicating a fixed language choice. The file does not offer any language selection or explain that the tool is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking context, which conflicts with the policy against forcing a specific language without opt-in.","remediation":"Add a documented language/locale option or clearly state that the tool is intended for a specific Chinese-language environment. If multilingual use is expected, provide bilingual or selectable user-facing messages and help text.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/deduplicate.py","start_line":3,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-da18b11167a14974b4080b5e56fa1167","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/organize.py","start_line":2,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language strings that present the tool exclusively in Chinese, including the module docstring and later CLI messages. Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without offering a choice or documenting a justified locale restriction is a policy violation.","remediation":"Provide multilingual support or let the user choose the interface language via arguments, environment settings, or locale detection with opt-in. Alternatively, document a clear justified reason that the tool is intentionally Chinese-only.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/organize.py","start_line":2,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-0045f2b961f7423894ed7c1b7eff1a14","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"scripts/sync.py","start_line":2,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"The top-level docstring states that the tool supports both one-way mirror synchronization and bidirectional synchronization. In contrast, the sync_bidirectional function only prints that the feature is under development and performs no synchronization, which is a direct contradiction between documentation and behavior.","remediation":"Revise the docstring to accurately describe current capabilities, or implement the advertised bidirectional sync behavior so the documentation matches the code.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/sync.py","start_line":2,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-fbaaa85a7a524cc991bb35472f9eef52","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/sync.py","start_line":3,"end_line":5},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file presents its description, prompts, status messages, and CLI guidance only in Chinese, which imposes a locale/language choice on users. The policy allows language constraints only when users can opt in or when the limitation is clearly justified, neither of which is present here.","remediation":"Add multilingual support or a language-selection option, or clearly document that this skill is intended only for a specific Chinese-language context and why that restriction is necessary.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/sync.py","start_line":3,"end_line":5}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-9e3a2c56df27463ba17dee51330461b7","c